1. Create EC2 instance in your sandbox
2. Make sure that port 22, 90 are open in it's security group
3. Install nginx using dnf ( dnf install nginx)
4. edit it's config file to make listen on port 90 
5. create /usr/share/nginx/xyz directory
6. add index file in the newly created directly including your name
7. edit nginx config file to update the root dir to /usr/share/nginx/xyz
8. run "nginx -t" to check nginx config sytax
9. run "systemctl reload nginx" to reload nginx
10. open duckdns.org and create a record with yourname or whatever you want and make it point to the Ec2 public IP
11. access the server using the domain and port 90
12. send me a screenshot from the nginx.conf and from the server accessed